 "message": "A 12-frame, one-shot golden light pillar: a small glow at the ground first (anticipation), then a full bright beam with a cross-shaped flare and a ground ring at the peak, then the beam thins, sparks fly and a grey smoke puff rises and fades. The beam width, ring size and cross length are the main sliders to tune; I did not add a dark outline because the glow reads better without one, and the smoke is small.",
